00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:29.290
Won't you sit down, George?

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:29.910
No, thank you.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:34.170
I'm going to be very brief and to the point.

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:39.190
It's about my Eddie and your boy, I believe the kids call him Gopher.

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:41.290
Beaver.

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:42.400
Beaver, yes.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:43.390
What's he done?

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:50.620
Ward, you know me fairly well.

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:55.370
You've known me as a level-headed, conservative fellow, right?

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:56.490
Right.

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:56.950
Right.

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:03.140
Ward, your beaver has put a voodoo curse on my Eddie.

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:09.120
Well, have you called in a good witch doctor yet?

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:14.680
Ward, I'm just giving you the facts.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.810
One, Eddie's in great pain in his stomach and his chest.

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.270
Two, the doctor says that there's nothing wrong with him,

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:21.200
but he can see.

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:24.790
Three, your beaver has made a black magic doll

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:25.650
and stuck pins in it.

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:29.820
Well, must be some kind of a joke, George.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.100
Well, it's no joke to me or to Eddie's mother.

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:36.360
Well, we'd, uh, we'd better do something about that, huh?

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.220
Excuse me, George.

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:42.280
Well, maybe you and George would like a cup of coffee.

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:42.860
Where are you going?

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:45.470
Gonna see if Beaver put a voodoo curse on Eddie.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:46.380
Oh.

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:55.860
Well, George, would you like a cup of coffee?

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:57.460
Uh...

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:01.750
I believe none.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:05.140
Oh, hi, Dad.

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:05.840
Hi, Dad.

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:06.680
Hi.

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:11.410
Beaver, uh, Mr. Haskell is downstairs,

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:12.410
and he's pretty upset.

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:15.040
Did you get a doll of Eddie and stick pins in it?

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:16.730
I got it right here, Dad.

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:22.120
Good gosh, Beaver.

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:26.170
Beaver, did you ever do anything like this before?

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:27.990
No, this is my first time.

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:29.820
I guess that's why it didn't work.

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:33.730
I told him it was silly, Dad.

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:35.670
Is there something wrong with Daddy?

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:37.420
He was all right this afternoon.

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:40.760
Yes, it seems he has pains in his chest and stomach.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.380
How could he be sick, Dad?

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:47.300
I took the pin and the nail out and then cursed him.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.150
Well, we'll talk about that later.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:54.590
Right now, I think I'd better get back downstairs

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:56.610
and see what I can do about calming Mr. Haskell down.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.680
George, I just can't believe this.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:03.380
The beaver's such a sweet little fellow.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:05.940
Well, he likes everybody, even Eddie.

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:08.980
I mean, he likes everybody.

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:11.840
Well?

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:14.480
I was just telling George here that the beaver wouldn't

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:16.120
think of doing anything like this.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:20.520
Yes, well, it seems he did stick some pins in a doll.

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:22.650
Then it's true.

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:24.740
What are you going to do about this, Ward?

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:26.040
Wait a minute, George.

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:27.520
Let's be sensible about this.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:28.500
We're both adults.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:29.980
We know there's no such thing as black.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.380
I don't know about these things,

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:34.420
but the fact remains that Eddie has pains

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:35.660
in his stomach and in his chest.

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:38.560
Well, then they must be psychological pains, George.

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:41.680
Look, you see, Eddie believed it would work, so it worked.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:44.420
That's the whole secret of the witch doctor's power.

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:46.660
You seem to know a great deal about this subject.

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:48.020
Yeah, I've read a little about it.

00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:49.260
I'm sure you have.

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:51.280
Your son must have picked it up somewhere,

00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:53.060
and it's not in the school curriculum.

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:56.240
George, the whole thing came from a picture the boy saw.

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:59.500
Look, George, let's keep our feet on the ground.

00:20:59.500 --> 00:20:59.880
on these.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:02.050
pains of Eddie's are in his mind.

00:21:02.330 --> 00:21:03.170
No, they're not.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:04.730
They're in his stomach and in his chest.

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:06.510
And I expect you to do something about it.

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:08.110
And don't ask me what.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:08.850
Good night.

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:17.790
Good night, Joan.

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:21.140
Yes, George, and say hello to Agnes for me.

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:23.060
Yeah.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.300
Well, you may have something there, Agnes.

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:43.870
Well, I'm so glad to hear that Eddie's back on his feet.

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:45.480
Thanks for calling.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:46.540
Goodbye.

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:48.480
Hi.

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:49.640
Hello, dear.

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:51.040
That was Agnes Haskell.

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:52.650
Eddie's feeling fine again.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:53.270
Oh, yeah.

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:53.970
I thought he would be.

00:21:54.150 --> 00:21:55.510
How long before dinner?

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:57.180
About 10 minutes.

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:03.660
Was you so sure that Eddie was going to be all right?

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:05.760
Oh, I told you I'd take care of it, and I did.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:08.500
I had a little talk with Beaver last night.

00:22:09.820 --> 00:22:12.920
Well, what did the beaver say to Eddie that cured him?

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:16.120
Well, June, I told you I'd read a little on the subject.

00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:20.460
So I sent the beaver over with a genuine voodoo curse remover.

00:22:25.440 --> 00:22:27.240
A voodoo curse remover?

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:28.150
Well, sure.

00:22:28.670 --> 00:22:29.970
You can find the ingredients for that.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:31.620
I hadn't any good black magic cookbook.

00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:33.210
What's in it?

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:37.630
Well, you take three worms from the backyard,

00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:39.990
four hares from a dog's tail,

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:42.670
six toadstools picked in the light of the moon,

00:22:42.830 --> 00:22:44.830
two hares from a small boy's head.

00:22:44.950 --> 00:22:46.490
Uh, that hurt the beaver a little bit,

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:47.790
but I figured he had it coming to him.

00:22:48.890 --> 00:22:51.390
And you put all of the ingredients in a bull Durham sack,

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:53.790
and you pass it six times over the victim's body.

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:56.250
And I told the beaver that he could recite any magic words

00:22:56.250 --> 00:22:56.910
that came to mind.

00:22:57.940 --> 00:22:59.980
Oh, boy. It's...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.760
wonderful having a practicing witch doctor in the family

00:23:02.760 --> 00:23:03.480
when you need him.

00:23:05.100 --> 00:23:17.680
Hey, June, you know that drive in the country

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:18.960
I was talking about last Saturday?

00:23:19.320 --> 00:23:20.460
What do you say we try it again today?

00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:23.130
Eddie Haskell's upstairs.

00:23:23.600 --> 00:23:24.840
Boys are going to the movies again.

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:25.980
Eddie Haskell.

00:23:28.280 --> 00:23:29.960
You think I ought to drop a few jen-

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.980
hint to the boys that maybe Eddie Haskell is not the ideal American youth.

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:35.780
Oh, honey, that's the worst thing you can do.

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:38.440
Let them find out for themselves. They will soon enough.

00:23:38.680 --> 00:23:41.380
Hey, fellas, let's go to the Globe again this week.

00:23:41.540 --> 00:23:43.180
They got a couple of great pictures.

00:23:43.830 --> 00:23:46.430
Monsters from outer space and the thing that creeps.

00:23:46.680 --> 00:23:48.420
Look, Eddie, we told you before.

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:51.360
Mom doesn't want me taking Beaver to those kind of pictures.

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:53.300
What's the matter with you guys?

00:23:53.560 --> 00:23:56.680
You would never catch me listening to my parents. I never do.

00:23:56.880 --> 00:23:59.920
Yeah, Eddie. Well, maybe that's why you're such a miserable creep.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.380
That's why you're such a miserable creep.

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:07.990
I don't care where you're going, but me and the Beaver are going to the Valencia.

00:24:08.270 --> 00:24:16.810
Come on, Beave. Bye, Dad.

00:24:17.950 --> 00:24:18.490
Bye, Dad.

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:19.890
Where are you boys going?

00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:21.140
The Valencia.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:22.160
To see Pinocchio.

00:24:25.140 --> 00:24:26.080
Goodbye, Mrs. Cleaver.

00:24:26.240 --> 00:24:27.280
Goodbye, Mr. Cleaver.

00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:27.740
Bye, Eddie.

00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:29.960
Eddie, aren't you going to movies with the boys?

00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:33.570
Well, I wasn't, but I guess I will go to the Valencia.

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:35.760
I think that's what my parents would like.

00:24:43.240 --> 00:24:45.820
Well, looks like there might be some hope for Eddie too, huh?
